  "statement": "One family as sixteen left-handed Weyl fields (the even patterns): the symmetric bilinear forms of the mode operators that conserve colour and electric charge are six: four Dirac terms, the pairing of the neutral singlet with itself and the pairing of the left neutrino with itself. Exactly one is invariant under the twelve responses: the singlet pairing; it is also invariant under the degree and under each of the five level numbers. Without the singlet (the fifteen states of the audit) no invariant form exists and three Higgs channels remain; with it there are four Higgs channels and one bare term. Labelled by the odd patterns instead, the same pairing carries degree ten: the two labellings differ by five units of fermion number per field."
